## 4. Database Schema (v4)

```sql
images            — canonical image records
  id              INTEGER PK AUTOINCREMENT
  file_path       TEXT UNIQUE          -- absolute normalised path
  sha256          TEXT UNIQUE          -- exact dedup key
  phash           TEXT                 -- perceptual hash (near-dedup)
  width / height  INTEGER
  format          TEXT                 -- PNG / JPEG / WEBP …
  capture_source  TEXT                 -- steam | xbox | nvidia | amd | manual
  capture_ts      TEXT                 -- ISO-8601 (EXIF or mtime fallback)
  file_mtime      TEXT NOT NULL        -- OS mtime
  exif_json       TEXT                 -- raw EXIF as JSON blob
  colour_palette  TEXT                 -- [migration v2] dominant colours
  similarity_vec  BLOB                 -- [migration v3] embedding vector
  user_notes      TEXT                 -- [migration v4] free-form notes
  is_duplicate    INTEGER DEFAULT 0    -- 0=canonical, 1=duplicate
  duplicate_of    INTEGER → images(id)
  status          TEXT DEFAULT 'new'   -- new | indexed | classified | error
  ingested_at     TEXT                 -- auto ISO-8601
  last_seen_at    TEXT                 -- updated on every scan pass

tags              — tag vocabulary (system + user + ml)
image_tags        — many-to-many with confidence score and source
sources           — watched directories/drives
ingestion_runs    — audit log per scan
ml_results        — raw model outputs per image
schema_migrations — version history
```

