## 5. Threading Model

```
Main thread (Qt event loop)
│
├─ MissionControllerWidget + all UI panels
├─ QueryAPI calls (short-lived DB reads; thread-local connection)
│
└─ QtBatchWorker.start() ──► spawns worker thread
   │
   └─ BatchIngestionWorker._run() [daemon thread]
      │
      ├─ DedupEngine, MetadataExtractor, ImageIngestor, SceneClassifier
      ├─ All DB writes (thread-local connection per thread)
      └─ ProgressBus.publish(event) ──► QtBatchWorker._on_event()
                                              │
                                         emits Qt signals (queued connections)
                                              │
                                    MonitorPanel / ControlPanel slots
                                    (back on main thread — safe for UI updates)
```

**Safety rules:**
- `DatabaseManager` uses `threading.local()` — each thread gets its own connection.
- `ProgressBus` uses `threading.Lock()` around subscriber list.
- Qt signals from worker thread → UI are automatically queued by Qt's event loop.
- `stop_flag` is a single-element mutable list `[False]` — shared reference, no lock needed for a single bool.

